 - schedule() - Main scheduling function\nsrc/index.ts - Re-export\nsrc/scheduler.test.ts - Tests\n```\n\nFor the `schedule` function:\n1. Validate inputs (detect cycles)\n2. Compute topological order with heuristic ordering within levels\n3. Greedy assignment\n4. Optimization pass (try to fit unscheduled events)\n5. Return result\n\nLet me code it now.\n\nActually, I just realized I should think about one more thing: the \"maximizing\" requirement. What if I implement a backtracking solver but with a limit on the number of nodes explored? If the limit is reached, return the best solution found so far.\n\nThis is a good compromise between correctness and performance. Let me implement it.\n\nThe key is to set the limit high enough to find good solutions for typical inputs, but low enough to avoid timeouts.\n\nLet me use a node limit of 100,000. For most practical inputs, the backtracking will find the optimal solution well within this limit.\n\nOK here's my final implementation:\n\n```typescript\n// Backtracking solver with node limit\nconst NODE_LIMIT = 100000;\nlet nodesExplored = 0;\n\nfunction solve(\n  events: Event[],\n  index: number,\n  state: SolverState,\n  validRooms: Map<string, Room[]>,\n  gap: number,\n  options: ScheduleOptions,\n  best: BestResult\n): void {\n  if (nodesExplored >= NODE_LIMIT) return;\n  nodesExplored++;\n  \n  if (index >= events.length) {\n    if (state.scheduledCount > best.count) {\n      best.count = state.scheduledCount;\n      best.assignments = new Map(state.assignments);\n    }\n    return;\n  }\n  \n  // Pruning\n  const remaining = events.length - index;\n  if (state.scheduledCount + remaining <= best.count) return;\n  \n  const event = events[index];\n  \n  // Check prerequisites\n  let earliestStart = options.startTime;\n  let prereqMet = true;\n  if (event.prerequisites) {\n    for (const prereqId of event.prerequisites) {\n      const prereqAssign = state.assignments.get(prereqId);\n      if (!prereqAssign) {\n        prereqMet = false;\n        break;\n      }\n      earliestStart = Math.max(earliestStart, prereqAssign.endTime + gap);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Try to schedule the event\n  let scheduled = false;\n  if (prereqMet && earliestStart + event.duration <= options.endTime) {\n    const rooms = validRooms.get(event.id) ?? [];\n    \n    for (const room of rooms) {\n      const roomAssignments = state.roomSchedule.get(room.id) ?? [];\n      const slot = findEarliestSlot(roomAssignments, earliestStart, event.duration, gap, options.endTime);\n      \n      if (slot !== null) {\n        scheduled = true;\n        const placement = { roomId: room.id, startTime: slot, endTime: slot + event.duration };\n        \n        // Place\n        state.assignments.set(event.id, placement);\n        const roomList = state.roomSchedule.get(room.id);\n        if (!roomList) {\n          state.roomSchedule.set(room.id, [placement]);\n        } else {\n          insertSorted(roomList, placement);\n        }\n        state.scheduledCount++;\n        \n        solve(events, index + 1, state, validRooms, gap, options, best);\n        \n        // Unplace\n        state.assignments.delete(event.id);\n        if (roomList) {\n          const idx = roomList.findIndex(p => \n            p.roomId === placement.roomId && p.startTime === placement.startTime\n          );\n          if (idx >= 0) roomList.splice(idx, 1);\n        }\n        state.scheduledCount--;\n        \n        // Early termination\n        if (best.count === events.length || nodesExplored >= NODE_LIMIT) return;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Try not scheduling this event\n  // Only try this if it might lead to a better solution\n  // (i.e., if there are still enough remaining events to potentially beat the best)\n  if (state.scheduledCount + (events.length - index - 1) > best.count) {\n    solve(events, index + 1, state, validRooms, gap, options, best);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait, I realize there's a problem with the \"try not scheduling\" 